# docs/ — the yamlover documentation book: a directory chapter (the examples/66 shape).
# Each toplevel chapter is a subdirectory with its own .yo/body.yo; this root body holds the
# intro prose and orders the chapters. Sources and migration progress: ../DOCSMIGRATION.md.
!!<*yamlover: $defs: chapter>
yamlover
description: YAML with pointers — the language, its storage model, and its documents
- |
  **yamlover** is a language close to YAML that adds a *pointer layer* — `*` dereferences,
  `&` path anchors, keys that are pointers — and *concretes*: the same logical document can
  live in one file, in a directory tree, or switch language mid-stream. What YAML gives one
  file, yamlover gives a whole filesystem.
- |
  This book is the reference. It is itself a yamlover document tree — every page here is a
  chapter, every paragraph a marklower chunk, and the table of contents is the positional
  body you are reading now.
- *: language
- *: pointers
- *: types
- *: concretes
- *: query
- *: documents
